              <fr:mainmatter>
                <html:p>
    An embedded <fr:link href="/dhsorens-lean/" title="The Lean Theorem Prover" uri="https://derekhsorensen.com/dhsorens-lean/" display-uri="dhsorens-lean" type="local">Lean</fr:link> DSL for writing zk circuits against <fr:link href="/dhsorens-002U/" title="AIR" uri="https://derekhsorensen.com/dhsorens-002U/" display-uri="dhsorens-002U" type="local">AIR</fr:link>, Plonkish, and <fr:link href="/dhsorens-002S/" title="R1CS" uri="https://derekhsorensen.com/dhsorens-002S/" display-uri="dhsorens-002S" type="local">R1CS</fr:link>, built by zkSecurity under a verified-zkEVM grant. Circuit, specification, and proof live in the same file — an arrangement <fr:link href="/dhsorens-001J/" title="Smart Contract Specification" uri="https://derekhsorensen.com/dhsorens-001J/" display-uri="dhsorens-001J" type="local">smart contract verification</fr:link> has never had.
</html:p>
                <html:p>
    Questions this page should answer:
    <html:ul><html:li>How a circuit is represented, and what the proof obligation looks like — the precise form of "this circuit is sound with respect to this specification".</html:li>
        <html:li><fr:link href="/dhsorens-004T/" title="Completeness" uri="https://derekhsorensen.com/dhsorens-004T/" display-uri="dhsorens-004T" type="local">Completeness</fr:link> as a separate obligation, and whether it is discharged or assumed.</html:li>
        <html:li>Lookups and VM-like table ensembles: the recent generalisation, and what it makes provable end to end.</html:li>
        <html:li>Witness generation by compilation to an intermediate representation, and whether the generator is verified against the constraints.</html:li>
        <html:li>Backends — plonky3 now, stwo and R1CS variants planned — and what a backend has to guarantee.</html:li>
        <html:li>How Clean's circuit specs should meet <fr:link href="/dhsorens-0040/" title="ArkLib" uri="https://derekhsorensen.com/dhsorens-0040/" display-uri="dhsorens-0040" type="local">ArkLib</fr:link>'s protocol specs. It is the load-bearing seam between the two libraries.</html:li></html:ul></html:p>
