            <fr:title text="The Sumcheck Protocol">The Sumcheck Protocol</fr:title>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p>
    One protocol, used everywhere: GKR, <fr:link href="/dhsorens-003G/" title="Spartan and Sumcheck-Based SNARKs" uri="https://derekhsorensen.com/dhsorens-003G/" display-uri="dhsorens-003G" type="local">Spartan</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/dhsorens-003H/" title="HyperPlonk and the Multilinear Turn" uri="https://derekhsorensen.com/dhsorens-003H/" display-uri="dhsorens-003H" type="local">HyperPlonk</fr:link>, Basefold, logUp-GKR, <fr:link href="/dhsorens-003C/" title="WHIR" uri="https://derekhsorensen.com/dhsorens-003C/" display-uri="dhsorens-003C" type="local">WHIR</fr:link>. It is the first thing <fr:link href="/dhsorens-0040/" title="ArkLib" uri="https://derekhsorensen.com/dhsorens-0040/" display-uri="dhsorens-0040" type="local">ArkLib</fr:link> formalised, and probably the right place to start reading Lean.
</html:p>
            <html:p>
    Questions this page should answer:
    <html:ul><html:li>The protocol and <fr:link href="/dhsorens-004L/" title="Round-by-Round Soundness" uri="https://derekhsorensen.com/dhsorens-004L/" display-uri="dhsorens-004L" type="local">its soundness error</fr:link>, stated with the degree and variable count explicit.</html:li>
        <html:li>Prover cost: the linear-time algorithm, and what changes when the base field is small.</html:li>
        <html:li>Batching several sumchecks; zero-knowledge variants.</html:li>
        <html:li>Reducing a claim about a polynomial to an evaluation — the interface by which sumcheck meets a <fr:link href="/dhsorens-002Z/" title="Polynomial Commitment Schemes" uri="https://derekhsorensen.com/dhsorens-002Z/" display-uri="dhsorens-002Z" type="local">commitment scheme</fr:link>.</html:li>
        <html:li>Why the <fr:link href="/dhsorens-002G/" title="Fiat–Shamir and the Random Oracle Model" uri="https://derekhsorensen.com/dhsorens-002G/" display-uri="dhsorens-002G" type="local">Fiat–Shamir attack</fr:link> landed on GKR, a sumcheck-based protocol, and what that implies about parameterisation.</html:li></html:ul></html:p>
            <html:p>
